      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's possible that your engagement patterns are being interpreted by automated moderation or recommendation systems in ways you don't intend. Algorithms are indeed designed to promote \"cohesive\" interaction, which can unintentionally flag unique communication styles as unusual activity. This doesn't necessarily mean you're being personally attacked, but rather that your contributions might be falling outside the established behavioral norms the system is optimized to recognize. Keep observing *when* this happens relative to specific actions, as that might give a clue to the trigger.",
